{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1302178-changeling-in-other-languages","id":1302178,"title":"Changeling in other languages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-03T06:06:57-07:00","id":1302178,"title":"Changeling in other languages","content":"Let's get homebrew translations going.<br /> <br /> I think I'm not the only one who has run Changeling in a language other than English (in my case Swedish) and I thought that maybe I'm not the only one who has translated the specific words of the game, the lexicon, or at least some of it, to that language. I searched for a place where maybe that was already covered, but I found none, so I made a topic for it here. Feel free to use these, and submit your own versions. I'll update this original post with any contributions in any language.<br /> <br /> Notes!<br /> I contract the submissions to words, conjugations and really relevant stuff to keep down word count and stuff.<br /> <br /> English &gt; Swedish<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Dictionary by Spinnerling</b><br /> Arcadia - Arkadia, Alfheim, \u00c4lvlandet<br /> Changeling - Bortbyting<br /> Court - Hov<br /> Fae, True Fae, Fairies, Gentry - \u00c4lvor<br /> Fetch - Verk (ett verk, flera verk, de verken)<br /> Freehold - Fristad<br /> Gateway - Port<br /> Hedge, the - Sn\u00e5ret<br /> Hedgespun - Sn\u00e5rspunnet<br /> Hollow - Gl\u00e4nta<br /> Keeper - V\u00e4ktare<br /> Mask - Sl\u00f6ja<br /> Trod - Stig</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> English &gt; Arabic<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Dictionary by Shawarbaaz</b><br /> Arcadia - Firdous<br /> Beast - Mutawahish<br /> Darkling - Kayiyb<br /> Elemental - Jawhar<br /> Fairest - Eadhra<br /> Fetch - Qareen<br /> Goblin - Qazam<br /> Goblin market - souk al'aqzam<br /> Hedge, the - al-Malakut<br /> Huntsman - siad<br /> Ogre - shabh<br /> Privateer - qursan<br /> Thorns, the - al Ashwak<br /> True Fae - Djinn<br /> Wizened - Dhabil</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> English &gt; German<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Dictionary by Ventrue Life</b><br /> Changeling - Wechselbalg<br /> Court - Gericht<br /> Fae, True Fae, Fairies - Fee, Wahre Feen, Elfen<br /> Fetch - Geholt<br /> Freehold - Freier Halt<br /> Gateway - Tor (gate), Durchgang (gateway) or Zugang (entrance)<br /> Goblin, Hobgoblin - Kobold<br /> Hedge - Hecke, Einfassung<br /> Hedgespinning - Heckenspinnen<br /> Hollow - Hohl<br /> Keeper - Betreuer<br /> Mask - Maske<br /> Mien - Miene<br /> Trod - Getreten<br /> <br /> <b>Dictionary by Dead Guy</b><br /> court- Hof<br /> Fetch - Geholter<br /> Freehold - Freischaft<br /> Gateway - Torweg, Tor (gate), Durchgang (gateway), Zugang (entrance)<br /> Hollow - Aush\u00f6lung<br /> Keeper - W\u00e4rter , Halter<br /> Trod - Trampelpfad<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> English &gt; French<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Dictionary by BetterWorldz</b><br /> Arcadia - Arcadia, Arcadie<br /> Beast - Bestial<br /> Bedlam - Tumulte (Official C:tD French translation, had to change that Crown 'Tumult' contract to 'Tourmente' [Torment])<br /> Bridge Burners - Coupeurs de ponts<br /> Changeling - Changelin<br /> Clarity - Clart\u00e9<br /> Cold Iron - Fer Froid<br /> Darkling - Sombre<br /> Durance - Captivit\u00e9<br /> Elemental - \u00c9l\u00e9mentaire<br /> Entitlement - Attitrement<br /> Fae - Fae<br /> Fairest - Sublime<br /> Fetch - Simulacre<br /> Freehold - Fief<br /> Gentry - Aristocrates, Aristocrates Arcadiens<br /> Glamour - Glamour, F\u00e9erie<br /> Goblin Contract/Fruit/Market - Contrat/Fruit/March\u00e9 Gobelin<br /> Hedge - La Haie<br /> Hedgespinning - Tisser la Haie<br /> Hedgespun - Tiss\u00e9 dans la Haie or just Tiss\u00e9<br /> Hobgoblin - Gobelin<br /> Hollow - Refuge (small), Domaine (bigger)<br /> Keeper - Ma\u00eetre<br /> Kenning : Acuit\u00e9 (Official C:tD French translation)<br /> Kith - Kith<br /> Lost - \u00c9gar\u00e9<br /> Loyalist - Loyaliste<br /> Mantle - Manteau<br /> Mask - Masque<br /> Mien - Apparence f\u00e9erique<br /> Motley - Cercle<br /> Oath - Serment<br /> Ogres - Ogres<br /> Touchstone - Pillier (&quot;Pillar&quot;)<br /> Pledge - Promesse<br /> Portaling - L'\u00c9vasion<br /> Privateer - Esclavagiste<br /> Seeming - Aspect<br /> Thorns - Les \u00e9pines<br /> Token - Artefact<br /> Trod - Sentier (Official C:tD French translation)<br /> True Fae - Vraie Fae, Vraie F\u00e9e<br /> Wizened - Fl\u00e9tri<br /> Wyrd - Estrange (Medieval word for &quot;strange&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>Kiths by Monsieur Chat</b><br /> <br /> Elementals<br /> <br /> Fireheart: Coeur-de-flammes<br /> Snowskin: Peau-de-neige<br /> Eartbones: Os-du-sols<br /> Airtouched: Touche-de-brises<br /> Waterborn: N\u00e9-d'\u00e9cumes<br /> Woodblood: Sang-bois\u00e9<br /> Blightbent: Miasme-Serfs<br /> Metalflesh: Chair-m\u00e9tal<br /> Levinquick : Voltes-\u00c2mes<br /> Sandharrowed:Veines-de-Sables<br /> <br /> Beasts<br /> <br /> Broadback: Larges-\u00e9paules<br /> Hunterheart: \u00c2me-de-chasses<br /> Runnerswift: Vif-coureur<br /> Swimmerskin: Peau-d'\u00e9cailles<br /> Venombite: Mord-fiels<br /> Windwing: Aile-vents<br /> Cleareyes: Claire-pupilles,<br /> Coldscale: Froide-\u00e9cailles<br /> Roteater: Mange-corps<br /> TrueFriend: Coeur-fid\u00e8les<br /> Skitterskulk : Insecto\u00efdes<br /> Steepscrambler : Grimpeurs<br /> <br /> Darklings<br /> <br /> Antiquarians: Antiquaires<br /> Gravewight: \u00c2me-des-Cryptes<br /> Leechfingers: Vole-souffle<br /> Mirrorskin: Peau-Miroir<br /> Lurkglider: Hante-vent<br /> Moonborn: Enfant-lune<br /> Nightsinger: Chante-nuit<br /> Palewraith: Pale-esprit<br /> Razorhand: Main-rasoir<br /> Whisperwisp : Murmurant<br /> Tunnelgrub :Mo\u00eblles-de-Br\u00e8ches<br /> <br /> Ogres<br /> <br /> Gargantuan: Gargantuesques<br /> Cyclopeans: Cyclop\u00e9ens<br /> Farwalker: Errants<br /> Stonebone: Os-de-Roches<br /> Waterweller: Hante-l'eau<br /> Gistlegrinders : M\u00e2cheurs d\u2019os<br /> Bloodbrute: Sanglants<br /> witchtooh: Dent-de-sorci\u00e8re<br /> Corpsegrinder: Marche-cadavre<br /> <br /> Wizened<br /> <br /> Artist: Artiste<br /> Author: Auteur<br /> Brewer: Brasseur<br /> Chatelaine: Chatelain<br /> Chirurgeon: Chirurgien<br /> Drudge: T\u00e2cheron<br /> Gameplayer: Joueur<br /> Miner: Mineur<br /> Oracle: Oracle<br /> Smith: Forgeron<br /> Soldier: Soldat<br /> Woodwalker: Forestier</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13128,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","user":"Spinnerling","date":". 04-07-2019, 06:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T06:10:12-07:00","id":1302181,"title":"","content":"I made this for a Golden Age of Islam game I'm currently running.<br /> <br /> Arabic - English<br /> <br /> al Ashwak - the Thorns<br /> <br /> Dhabil - Wizened<br /> <br /> Djinn - True Fae<br /> <br /> Eadhra - Fairest<br /> <br /> Qareen - Fetch<br /> <br /> Firdous - Arcadia<br /> <br /> Jawhar - Elemental<br /> <br /> Kayiyb - Darkling<br /> <br /> al-Malakut - the Hedge<br /> <br /> Mutawahish - Beast<br /> <br /> qazam - Goblin<br /> <br /> qursan - privateer<br /> <br /> Shabh - Ogre<br /> <br /> siad - huntsman<br /> <br /> souk al'aqzam - goblin market<br /> <br /> -<br /> I also Homebrewed the Courts of the Crescent Moon, a court system that is less meteorological and more centered around creatures of Arabian myth: The Ifrit court, the Marid court, and the Ghul court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","user":"Shawarbaaz","date":". 04-03-2019, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T07:06:16-07:00","id":1302193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1302178-changeling-in-other-languages?p=1302181#post1302181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made this for a Golden Age of Islam game I'm currently running.<br /> <br /> Arabic - English<br /> <br /> al Ashwak - the Thorns<br /> <br /> Dhabil - Wizened<br /> <br /> Djinn - True Fae<br /> <br /> Eadhra - Fairest<br /> <br /> Qareen - Fetch<br /> <br /> Firdous - Arcadia<br /> <br /> Jawhar - Elemental<br /> <br /> Kayiyb - Darkling<br /> <br /> al-Malakut - the Hedge<br /> <br /> Mutawahish - Beast<br /> <br /> qazam - Goblin<br /> <br /> qursan - privateer<br /> <br /> Shabh - Ogre<br /> <br /> siad - huntsman<br /> <br /> souk al'aqzam - goblin market<br /> <br /> -<br /> I also Homebrewed the Courts of the Crescent Moon, a court system that is less meteorological and more centered around creatures of Arabian myth: The Ifrit court, the Marid court, and the Ghul court.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll turn it around in order so if anyone is looking for what Fae (or whichever word) is in Arabic, they'll be able to search for it alphabetically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T10:58:23-07:00","id":1302273,"title":"","content":"Since most fairy tales find their origin in Germanic folklore (or at least got popularized in Germany by the brothers Grimm), I'll throw in the translations to German, in case anyone is interested:<br /> <br /> <b>Arcadia</b> - Arcadia<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling</b> - Wechselbalg (which literally means 'switched baby')<br /> <br /> <b>Court</b> - Gericht<br /> <br /> <b>Fae, True Fae, Fairies</b> - Fee, Wahre Feen, Elfen<br /> <br /> <b>Fetch</b> - Geholt ('Geholt' is the literal German word for 'fetch', but this is not an accurate translation. The accurate translation for 'fetch' would be 'Wechselbalg', the same word used for changeling, because what we call a fetch in CtL <i>is</i> the changeling in Germanic folklore.)<br /> <br /> <b>Freehold</b> - Freier Halt<br /> <br /> <b>Gateway</b> - Tor (gate), Durchgang (gateway) or Zugang (entrance)<br /> <br /> <b>Goblin, Hobgoblin</b> - Kobold (yes, I know on most modern western fantasies Kobold are different creatures, but originally &quot;goblin&quot; was the English translation of the German word &quot;Kobold&quot;.)<br /> <br /> <b>Hedge</b> - Hecke, Einfassung ('die Hecke' is an accurate translation, but I personally feel that 'die Einfassung' is a more elegant translation, it captures what 'the Hedge' is better.)<br /> <br /> <b>Hedgespinning</b> - Heckenspinnen<br /> <br /> <b>Hollow</b> - Hohl<br /> <br /> <b>Keeper</b> - Betreuer<br /> <br /> <b>Mask</b> - Maske<br /> <br /> <b>Mien</b> - Miene<br /> <br /> <b>Trod</b> - Getreten<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Disclaimer:</b> I'm not German myself, I'm Dutch, but I have studied German and it's the 3rd best language I speak, read and write. If any actual German person reads this and has any issue with my translations, feel free to correct them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-03-2019, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T01:49:20-07:00","id":1302504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1302178-changeling-in-other-languages?p=1302273#post1302273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Fetch</b> - Geholt ('Geholt' is the literal German word for 'fetch', but this is not an accurate translation. The accurate translation for 'fetch' would be 'Wechselbalg', the same word used for changeling, because what we call a fetch in CtL <i>is</i> the changeling in Germanic folklore.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true for Swedish as well, but I'm thinking that the human and the fae lingo differs. Humans just have no separate words for the two, because from their perspective, they're indistinguishable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T08:08:19-07:00","id":1302553,"title":"","content":"Maybe they call themselves whatever is the local Equivalent of The Lost and call Fetches Changelings","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T18:52:56-07:00","id":1302980,"title":"","content":"It can be hard to find perfect fits in French so I tend to take a bit of creative license on occasions for some of those terms to sound more appealing. Would love some recommendation from any French speaker out here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Arcadia - Arcadia (personal preference although Arcadie is the French name of the Greek region)<br /> Beast - Bestial<br /> Bedlam - Tumulte (From the old official C:tD French translation, had to change that Crown 'Tumult' contract to 'Tourmente' [Torment])<br /> Bridge Burners - Coupeurs de ponts<br /> Changeling - Changelin<br /> Clarity - Clart\u00e9<br /> Cold Iron - Fer Froid<br /> Darkling - Sombre<br /> Durance - Captivit\u00e9<br /> Elemental - \u00c9l\u00e9mentaire<br /> Entitlement - Attitrement (That one was super hard to find, I'm a little afraid it might sound a bit like a silly made up word but it does appear in an 1845 dictionary. For first ed I just went with &quot;noble order&quot; [ordre noble] but that won't cut it anymore)<br /> Fae - Fae (Medieval French but it sounds way more relevant to C:tL than the current form &quot;f\u00e9e&quot; which has a bit of a Tinker Bell connotation)<br /> Fairest - Sublime<br /> Fetch - Simulacre (If you have to translate it but I just keep the same term in my games, it just works better)<br /> Freehold - Fief<br /> Gentry - Aristocrates or Aristocrates Arcadiens (Imperfect but I think it works)<br /> Glamour - Glamour (Unfortunately in French the term only has the modern connotation so some might prefer to translate it with something such as F\u00e9erie)<br /> Goblin Contract/Fruit/Market - Contrat/Fruit/March\u00e9 Gobelin<br /> Hedge - La Haie<br /> Hedgespinning - Tisser la Haie (Imperfect)<br /> Hedgespun - Tiss\u00e9 dans la Haie or just Tiss\u00e9 (spun) to make it less clunky (Very imperfect)<br /> Hobgoblin - Gobelin<br /> Hollow - Refuge if small or Domaine if bigger (Never was able to nail that one)<br /> Keeper - Ma\u00eetre (To make it sound more like &quot;keeper of a pet&quot;)<br /> Kenning : Acuit\u00e9 (From the old official C:tD French translation)<br /> Kith - Kith (Never managed to translate it and it's been a problem as the French pronunciation makes it sound either as &quot;kit&quot;, &quot;kiss&quot; or &quot;kiffe&quot; [slang for liking something])<br /> Lost - \u00c9gar\u00e9<br /> Loyalist - Loyaliste<br /> Mantle - Manteau<br /> Mask - Masque<br /> Mien - Apparence f\u00e9erique<br /> Motley - Cercle (Imperfect)<br /> Oath - Serment<br /> Ogres - Ogres<br /> Touchstone - Pillier (&quot;Pillar&quot;, as the litteral &quot;pierre de touche&quot; just doesn't work in French)<br /> Pledge - Promesse<br /> Portaling - L'\u00c9vasion (Very imperfect but everything else I came up with sounded silly)<br /> Privateer - Esclavagiste<br /> Seeming - Aspect<br /> Thorns - Les \u00e9pines<br /> Token - Artefact (Never managed to coin that one either so I just fall back to plain old artifact)<br /> Trod - Sentier (From the old official C:tD French translation)<br /> True Fae - Vraie Fae or Vraie F\u00e9e<br /> Wizened - Fl\u00e9tri<br /> Wyrd - Estrange (Medieval form of &quot;\u00e9trange&quot; which means strange. Sticking to the more modern &quot;weird&quot; connotation rather than &quot;fate&quot; although I'll sometimes throw in &quot;Estrange Destin\u00e9e&quot; to salvage the concept as much as possible)<br /> <br /> I also always refer these wonderful 1e kith translations which come almost entirely from user Monsieur Chat on a French message board from a decade back, they're a great help to this day.<br /> <br /> Elementals<br /> <br /> Fireheart: Coeur-de-flammes<br /> Snowskin: Peau-de-neige<br /> Eartbones: Os-du-sols<br /> Airtouched: Touche-de-brises<br /> Waterborn: N\u00e9-d'\u00e9cumes<br /> Woodblood: Sang-bois\u00e9<br /> Blightbent: Miasme-Serfs<br /> Metalflesh: Chair-m\u00e9tal<br /> Levinquick : Voltes-\u00c2mes<br /> Sandharrowed:Veines-de-Sables<br /> <br /> Beasts<br /> <br /> Broadback: Larges-\u00e9paules<br /> Hunterheart: \u00c2me-de-chasses<br /> Runnerswift: Vif-coureur<br /> Swimmerskin: Peau-d'\u00e9cailles<br /> Venombite: Mord-fiels<br /> Windwing: Aile-vents<br /> Cleareyes: Claire-pupilles,<br /> Coldscale: Froide-\u00e9cailles<br /> Roteater: Mange-corps<br /> TrueFriend: Coeur-fid\u00e8les<br /> Skitterskulk : Insecto\u00efdes<br /> Steepscrambler : Grimpeurs<br /> <br /> Darklings<br /> <br /> Antiquarians: Antiquaires<br /> Gravewight: \u00c2me-des-Cryptes<br /> Leechfingers: Vole-souffle<br /> Mirrorskin: Peau-Miroir<br /> Lurkglider: Hante-vent<br /> Moonborn: Enfant-lune<br /> Nightsinger: Chante-nuit<br /> Palewraith: Pale-esprit<br /> Razorhand: Main-rasoir<br /> Whisperwisp : Murmurant<br /> Tunnelgrub :Mo\u00eblles-de-Br\u00e8ches<br /> <br /> Ogres<br /> <br /> Gargantuan: Gargantuesques<br /> Cyclopeans: Cyclop\u00e9ens<br /> Farwalker: Errants<br /> Stonebone: Os-de-Roches<br /> Waterweller: Hante-l'eau<br /> Gistlegrinders : M\u00e2cheurs d\u2019os<br /> Bloodbrute: Sanglants<br /> witchtooh: Dent-de-sorci\u00e8re<br /> Corpsegrinder: Marche-cadavre<br /> <br /> Wizened<br /> <br /> Artist: Artiste<br /> Author: Auteur<br /> Brewer: Brasseur<br /> Chatelaine: Chatelain<br /> Chirurgeon: Chirurgien<br /> Drudge: T\u00e2cheron<br /> Gameplayer: Joueur<br /> Miner: Mineur<br /> Oracle: Oracle<br /> Smith: Forgeron<br /> Soldier: Soldat<br /> Woodwalker: Forestier<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T21:32:37-07:00","id":1303001,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1302178-changeling-in-other-languages?p=1302273#post1302273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>English &gt; German </b><i>(by Ventrue Life)</i><br /> Changeling - Wechselbalg<br /> Court - Gericht<br /> Fae, True Fae, Fairies - Fee, Wahre Feen, Elfen<br /> Fetch - Geholt<br /> Freehold - Freier Halt<br /> Gateway - Tor (gate), Durchgang (gateway) or Zugang (entrance)<br /> Goblin, Hobgoblin - Kobold<br /> Hedge - Hecke, Einfassung<br /> Hedgespinning - Heckenspinnen<br /> Hollow - Hohl<br /> Keeper - Betreuer<br /> Mask - Maske<br /> Mien - Miene<br /> Trod - Getreten</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> court- Hof<br /> Fetch - Geholter<br /> Freehold - Freischaft<br /> Gateway - just as above but also includes Torweg<br /> Hollow - Aush\u00f6lung ,<br /> Keeper - W\u00e4rter , Halter<br /> Trod - Trampelpfad<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","user":"DeadGuy","date":". 04-06-2019, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T12:54:53-08:00","id":1363841,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the necromancy, but I've been working on a setting in Wales, and wished to contribute my thoughts and translations of Changeling terms into Welsh:<ul><li>Crimbil - Changeling</li> <li>Y Colledig - The Lost</li> <li>Ellyll - Fae</li> <li>Tylwyth Teg - True Fae</li> <li>Bendith y Mamau - Another term for the True Fae, sometimes meant in reference specifically to Keepers (In addition, Welsh Begotten sometimes refer to themselves as <i>Bendith y Fam</i>.)</li> <li>Annwn - Arcadia</li> <li>Newid - Fetch</li> <li>Contract - Contract<ul><li>Contract Annwn - Arcadian Contract</li> <li>Contract Cwrt - Court Contract</li> <li>Contract Bwgan - Goblin Contract</li> </ul></li> <li>Teyrndlws (pl. <i>Teyrndlysau</i>) - Regalia</li> <li>Hudoliaeth - Glamour</li> <li>Hawlrydd - Freehold</li> <li>Cwrt - Court<ul><li>Cwrt y Gwanwyn - Spring Court</li> <li>Cwrt yr Haf - Summer Court</li> <li>Cwrt yr Hydref - Autumn Court</li> <li>Cwrt y Gaeaf - Winter Court</li> </ul></li> <li>Gwedd - Mien</li> <li>Rhith - Mask</li> <li>Y Berth - The Hedge</li> <li>Y Draen - The Thorns</li> <li>Twll - Hollow</li> <li>Rhagfur - Bastion</li> <li>Pwca - Hobgoblin</li> <li>Bwci-bo - Hedge Ghost</li> <li>Nyddu'r Berth - Hedgespinning</li> <li>Celfyddyd Freuddwyd - Dreamweaving</li> <li>C\u0175n Annwn - Huntsmen (also referred to as <i>Helwyr</i> or <i>Gwyrddmyn</i>) (Also the name of a Lodge of Ghost Wolves who've bound themselves to a True Fae)</li> <li>Dyled Bwgan - Goblin Debt</li> <li>Brenhines Fwgan - Goblin Queen</li> <li>Enw - Title</li> <li>Addewid - Pledge<ul><li>Tynged - Sealing</li> <li>Llw - Oath</li> <li>Bargen - Bargain</li> <li>Enwir - Oathbreaker</li> </ul></li> <li>Agwedd - Seeming (Traditionally, Welsh changelings use their Seemings as a title, eg, a Beast named Ceri might refer to herself as <i>Ceri Wyllt</i>.)<ul><li>Gwyllt - Beast</li> <li>Godywyll - Darkling</li> <li>Elfennol - Elemental</li> <li>Goreuwedd - Fairest</li> <li>Cawr - Ogre</li> <li>Coblyn - Wizened</li> </ul></li> <li>Cydnabod (colloquially shortened to <i>Cyd</i>) - Kith</li> <li>Ffawd - Wyrd</li> <li>Eglurdod - Clarity</li> <li>Adnabod - Kenning</li> <li>Tocyn - Token</li> <li>Ffrwyth Bwgan - Goblin Fruit</li> <li>Criglyn - Oddment</li> <li>Harlach - Bedlam</li> <li>Bregedd - Frailty<ul><li>Diofryd - Taboo</li> <li>Distryw - Bane</li> </ul></li> <li>Arawn - A powerful and gregarious True Fae. Some Autumn Court scholars theorize the Title might be shared among multiple Gentry.</li> <li>Gwyn ap Nudd - One of Arawn's other Titles</li> <li>Pwyll - A legendary changeling said to have secured an oath of friendship between Arawn and the kingdom of Dyfed</li> </ul>Some notes on my choices:<ul><li><i>Tynged</i> literally means &quot;destiny,&quot; but mythically is used in a similar manner to the Irish <i>geas</i>.</li> <li><i>Bregedd</i> means &quot;weakness&quot; but also &quot;frivolity,&quot; which I thought was an interesting double-entendre.</li> <li><i>Diofryd</i> is an oath of renunciation.</li> <li>I had quite a devil of a time with &quot;Bane.&quot; I settled on <i>Distryw</i> as it can mean &quot;destruction,&quot; &quot;ruin,&quot; or &quot;curse.&quot; I tried (and failed) to find an equivalent to the Irish <i>urbhaidh</i>.</li> <li>Welsh has quite a few words referring to goblin, ghost, and the like, so for those terms I went with whatever &quot;felt&quot; most appropriate or evocative.</li> <li><i>Coblyn</i> refers to small, ugly fairies who live in mines, similar to Knockers. I chose them as a translation for the Wizened because they lead polite humans to wealth.</li> <li><i>Gwyllt</i> literally means &quot;wild,&quot; but is also an epithet applied to the warrior Cyledr in the tale <i>Culhwc ac Olwen</i> after Gwyn ap Nudd makes him eat his father's heart, which drives him to madness. In general, I tried to find precedence in the <i>Mabinogion</i> for my translations.</li> <li><i>Cawr</i> means &quot;giant&quot; or &quot;devil.&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Darkling&quot; was difficult, but I finally settled on <i>Godywyll</i>, which means &quot;darksome,&quot; &quot;not clearly seen,&quot; or &quot;gloomy.&quot; I considered <i>Cysgod</i> (&quot;Shadow&quot;) as well.</li> <li><i>Goreuwedd</i> means &quot;best face.&quot; Incidentally, I think the Flowering Kith might be translated as <i>Blodeuwedd</i>, so a Fairest Flowering would be <i>Blodeuwedd Oreuwedd</i>.</li> <li>&quot;Kenning&quot; is derived from the Icelandic <i>kenna</i>, meaning &quot;to know&quot; or &quot;to recognize.&quot; <i>Adnabod </i>is the Welsh equivalent.</li> <li>There are a few different words that could be translated as &quot;Hedge.&quot; I went with <i>Perth</i> for its meanings of &quot;copse,&quot; &quot;thicket,&quot; and &quot;jungle.&quot; Other potential translations include <i>Cae</i> (&quot;field&quot;), <i>Bid</i> (&quot;bush&quot;), or <i>Coed</i> (&quot;forest&quot;).</li> <li>The Huntsmen probably don't refer to themselves as <i>C\u0175n Annwn</i>.</li> <li><i>Ellyll</i> is one of those words that can refer to a wide variety of supernatural beings.</li> <li>A changeling can also be called <i>plentyn newid</i> (&quot;swapped child&quot;). I got <i>crimbil</i> from John Rh\u0177s's book of Welsh and Manx folklore. <i>Fetch</i> comes from Irish folklore, although its etymology is unclear. It might be connected to the Old Norse <i>fylgja</i>, a spirit that accompanies a person throughout their life. <i>Newid</i> means &quot;exchange&quot; and I imagine Welsh Lost use it euphemistically. Translating terms for Changeling is tricky since not only is most of the lexicon connected to specific cultural myths, but also there are quite a few conceptual swappings that make attempting to map things to different languages a bit of a guessing game.</li> <li>Speaking of which, <i>Wyrd</i> is an Anglo-Saxon term for fate. The Welsh equivalent is technically <i>Tynged</i>, except it lacks the mythic personification as well as evocative homophony. <i>Coel</i> could potentially work for meaning both &quot;omen&quot; and &quot;reputation.&quot; Or maybe <i>Hudwaith</i> for meaning &quot;craftiness&quot; and &quot;trickery.&quot; Ultimately, I went for <i>Ffawd</i> for its meaning of &quot;good fortune&quot; as well as the potentially ironic &quot;happiness.&quot;</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":".  Added some more terms 01-28-2020, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T13:46:58-08:00","id":1363850,"title":"","content":"No need to apologize: this is one of those good threads for revival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T03:41:16-08:00","id":1363938,"title":"","content":"A few Swedish suggestions:<br /> Arcadia - Arkadien (lit. translation of the Greek region), Alvhem (modern version of Alfhem and Alfheim), Utg\u00e5rd (from Asatro, so really old term)<br /> Changelings - Knytt (basically, magical being)<br /> Contracts - Kontrakt (lit. translation)<br /> Goblins - V\u00e4ttar, Tomtar (probably fell into disuse after Santa Claus &quot;Tomten&quot; rose in poplularity), both are literal translations but the latter has more positive/helpful connotations<br /> True Fae - Troll (troll in Nordic folklore vary almost as much as trolls in pop culture), Oknytt (like Knytt but with more malevolent connotations)<br /> Keeper - R\u00e5dare (lit. ruler of a domain; older as well as dialectal form of r\u00e5, beings that were kinda the spirits of different domains or places in nature and could very well seduce, steal and/or eat people for various reasons depending on the various versions that exist in Nordic folklore)<br /> <br /> The duality of Knytt/Oknytt would imply some kinship but also antagonism between the two groups. Having those concepts built into the language may influence local Changeling politics and opinions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T15:32:50-08:00","id":1364419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1302178-changeling-in-other-languages?p=1363938#post1363938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goblins - V\u00e4ttar, Tomtar (probably fell into disuse after Santa Claus &quot;Tomten&quot; rose in poplularity), both are literal translations but the latter has more positive/helpful connotations<br /> True Fae - Troll (troll in Nordic folklore vary almost as much as trolls in pop culture), Oknytt (like Knytt but with more malevolent connotations)</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd translate &quot;goblins&quot; to<i> troll</i>, myself. <i>V\u00e4ttar</i> strongly implies small size, while the goblins of CtL are unified more by being tricky and unreliable. It also works a lot better as a prefix for terms such as <i>trollkontrakt </i>and <i>trollmarknad.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T16:59:23-08:00","id":1364434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1302178-changeling-in-other-languages?p=1364419#post1364419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd translate &quot;goblins&quot; to<i> troll</i>, myself. <i>V\u00e4ttar</i> strongly implies small size, while the goblins of CtL are unified more by being tricky and unreliable. It also works a lot better as a prefix for terms such as <i>trollkontrakt </i>and <i>trollmarknad.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Good points, and you definitely sold my on trollmarknad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-ca